  "document_type": "aset-seed-compatibility-profile",
  "guarantees": [
    "Component primitives create no authority, execution validity, or recognized Outcome except through their declared Seed mapping.",
    "Expectation admission and external-effect dispatch use different documents, gates, and Permits.",
    "Memory retrieval, Master planning, and AttractorDescriptor remain advisory.",
    "Complete ASET systems may compose independent internal or external components, but authoritative transitions remain conformant to Seed concepts, validity conditions, invariants and lifecycle distinctions.",
    "Components may perform the work; Seed determines when that work acquires authoritative ASET significance."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Compatibility is specified against Seed 0.1-rc12 candidate semantics; owner approval and exact-byte Seed rc12 freeze remain separate.",
    "This profile does not claim distributed consensus, physical-world truth, production key custody, or connector idempotency.",
    "Component integration alone does not establish ASET compatibility without conformance to the Seed semantic lifecycle."
  ],
